\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces DashboardContext: Reactive State Flow. Selection in any view propagates to downstream views; each interaction is logged with context (heatmap cell $\to $ concept + severity, KG node $\to $ node ID, etc.).}}{36}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dashboard_context}{{7}{36}{}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Condition A vs. Condition B Interface Comparison.} Control participants receive summary-only evidence while treatment participants use the full interactive dashboard, isolating the causal effect of visual analytics on educator reasoning quality.}}{37}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:condition_ab}{{8}{37}{}{figure.8}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {System Usability Scale Results (Mock Data).} Control (Condition A, text summary only) shows lower usability ($M=55.5$, SD=17.0, Grade D) compared to treatment (Condition B, full interactive dashboard, $M=68.6$, SD=12.0, Grade B). Effect size: Cohen's $d=0.88$. This pre-submission mock reflects expected between-condition differences; actual data will replace these values upon user study completion.}}{37}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sus_scores}{{9}{37}{}{figure.9}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Think-Aloud Qualitative Coding Frequencies (Mock Data).} Treatment (Condition B) participants verbalized evidence-based reasoning significantly more often than control (Condition A): Causal Attribution (CA) 11 vs. 2, Semantic Alignment (SA) 9 vs. 1, Trust Calibration (TC) 8 vs. 3. Treatment shows 4.2x higher total coding frequency (34 vs. 8 segments), indicating deeper interactive engagement with the co-auditing interface. Mock data reflects expected effect sizes; actual inter-rater reliability ($\kappa $) and frequencies to follow.}}{38}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:qualitative_themes}{{10}{38}{}{figure.10}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Primary Outcome: Semantic Alignment Pre/Post Improvement (Mock Data).} Control (Condition A) shows minimal rubric improvement (pre=$0.584$, post=$0.624$, $\Delta =0.039$). Treatment (Condition B) shows substantial semantic alignment improvement (pre=$0.589$, post=$0.733$, $\Delta =0.144$, $p<0.001$, highly significant), indicating that the interactive dashboard guides educators toward more comprehensive, evidence-grounded rubric refinement. Treatment improvement is 3.6x larger than control. This mock data reflects expected effect sizes; actual results will replace these values upon study completion.}}{39}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:primary_outcome}{{11}{39}{}{figure.11}{}}
